============================================================
1. CELERY SYSTEM OVERVIEW
============================================================
Celery provides asynchronous and scheduled background processing for:

- Email delivery
- Media processing (images, thumbnails)
- Voting tallying
- Audit logging
- Scheduled maintenance tasks

Celery uses:
- Redis as broker
- Redis or Postgres as result backend
- Multiple worker groups bound to specific queues
- Horizontal scaling based on queue load

All tasks must be:
- Idempotent
- Logged
- Role-safe
- Validated


============================================================
2. QUEUE STRUCTURE
============================================================

QUEUE NAME        PURPOSE
------------------------------------------------------------
email_queue       Email sending, newsletters, notifications
media_queue       Image processing, thumbnails, file ops
voting_queue      Vote tallying, monthly reports
audit_queue       Admin action logging, system events
maintenance_queue Scheduled cleanup, backups, pruning

Each queue is processed by dedicated worker deployments.


============================================================
3. WORKER GROUPS
============================================================

WORKER GROUP         QUEUES CONSUMED
------------------------------------------------------------
email_worker         email_queue
media_worker         media_queue
voting_worker        voting_queue
audit_worker         audit_queue
maintenance_worker   maintenance_queue

Workers run in separate K3s deployments for isolation.


============================================================
4. TASK CATEGORIES
============================================================

CATEGORY: EMAIL TASKS
------------------------------------------------------------
send_email_task
send_bulk_email_task
send_newsletter_task
send_member_notification_task

Responsibilities:
- Deliver transactional emails
- Deliver admin communications
- Deliver newsletters
- Retry on failure with exponential backoff


CATEGORY: MEDIA TASKS
------------------------------------------------------------
generate_thumbnail_task
optimize_image_task
process_photo_upload_task
archive_old_media_task

Responsibilities:
- Resize images
- Generate thumbnails
- Validate file types
- Move media to long-term storage


CATEGORY: VOTING TASKS
------------------------------------------------------------
tally_votes_task
generate_vote_report_task
close_monthly_vote_task

Responsibilities:
- Count votes
- Generate monthly voting summaries
- Lock voting periods
- Ensure integrity via DB constraints


CATEGORY: AUDIT TASKS
------------------------------------------------------------
record_admin_action_task
record_system_event_task
record_security_event_task

Responsibilities:
- Log admin actions (content changes, role changes)
- Log system events (errors, restarts)
- Log security events (failed logins, permission denials)


CATEGORY: MAINTENANCE TASKS
------------------------------------------------------------
cleanup_temp_files_task
prune_old_logs_task
backup_database_task
sync_staging_to_prod_task

Responsibilities:
- Remove unused files
- Prune old logs
- Trigger DB backups
- Sync staging → production (optional)


============================================================
5. TASK DESIGN RULES
============================================================

IDEMPOTENCY
-----------
Tasks must be safe to run multiple times without causing corruption.

RETRY POLICY
------------
- Default: 3 retries
- Backoff: exponential (2s, 4s, 8s)
- Hard failures logged to audit_queue

LOGGING
-------
Every task logs:
- task_name
- task_id
- start_time
- end_time
- duration
- status
- error (if any)

VALIDATION
----------
Tasks must validate:
- IDs (event_id, user_id, vote_id)
- File paths
- Email addresses
- Role permissions (if applicable)

NO SENSITIVE DATA
-----------------
Tasks must not log:
- passwords
- JWTs
- PII beyond user_id


============================================================
6. TASK FLOW EXAMPLES
============================================================

EMAIL FLOW
----------
FastAPI → email_queue → email_worker → SMTP → audit_queue

MEDIA FLOW
----------
FastAPI → media_queue → media_worker → storage → audit_queue

VOTING FLOW
-----------
FastAPI → voting_queue → voting_worker → Postgres → audit_queue

AUDIT FLOW
----------
FastAPI → audit_queue → audit_worker → Postgres

MAINTENANCE FLOW
----------------
Cron schedule → maintenance_queue → maintenance_worker → storage/DB


============================================================
7. SCHEDULING (CELERY BEAT)
============================================================

SCHEDULED TASKS
------------------------------------------------------------
Daily:
- cleanup_temp_files_task
- prune_old_logs_task

Weekly:
- generate_vote_report_task
- archive_old_media_task

Monthly:
- close_monthly_vote_task
- backup_database_task

Beat runs in its own deployment for reliability.


============================================================
8. DEPLOYMENT ARCHITECTURE
============================================================

K3s Deployments:
- email-worker-deployment
- media-worker-deployment
- voting-worker-deployment
- audit-worker-deployment
- maintenance-worker-deployment
- celery-beat-deployment

Each worker:
- Has its own replica count
- Scales independently
- Uses environment variables:
  - REDIS_URL
  - DATABASE_URL
  - LOG_LEVEL


============================================================
9. FAILURE HANDLING
============================================================

ON FAILURE:
-----------
- Log error to audit_queue
- Retry with backoff
- Notify admin (optional)
- Mark task as failed in result backend

CATASTROPHIC FAILURE:
---------------------
- Worker restarts automatically
- Alerts triggered via monitoring
- Failed tasks logged for review


============================================================
10. SECURITY & RBAC IN TASKS
============================================================

RULES:
------
- Tasks must not bypass RBAC
- Tasks must validate user roles when performing admin actions
- Tasks must never modify roles or permissions directly
- Sensitive tasks (voting, audit) must run under least-privilege DB user


============================================================
11. TASK VERSIONING & MIGRATIONS
============================================================

VERSIONING:
-----------
- Tasks versioned by filename + function name
- Breaking changes require new task name

MIGRATIONS:
-----------
- Old tasks deprecated but kept until queues drain
- New tasks deployed via Helm


============================================================
12. OBSERVABILITY
============================================================

METRICS:
--------
- Task throughput
- Task duration
- Queue length
- Worker CPU/memory
- Failure rate

DASHBOARDS:
-----------
- Worker health dashboard
- Queue backlog dashboard
- Voting activity dashboard
- Email delivery dashboard

ALERTS:
-------
